{"name":"Citrus Zest","hex":"#edc85a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"citrus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several shrubs or trees of the genus Citrus in the family Rutaceae.","The fruit of such plants, generally spherical, oblate, or prolate, consisting of an outer glandular skin (called zest), an inner white skin (called pith or albedo), and generally between 8 and 16 sectors filled with pulp consisting of cells with one end attached to the inner skin. Citrus fruits include orange, grapefruit, lemon, lime, and citron."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or similar to citrus plants or fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citrus"},{"term":"zest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The outer skin of a citrus fruit, used as a flavouring or garnish.","General vibrance of flavour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scrape the zest from a fruit.","To make more zesty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zest (ingredient)","blocks":[{"text":"Zest is a food ingredient that is prepared by scraping or cutting from the rind of unwaxed citrus fruits such as lemon, orange, citron, and lime. Zest is used to add flavor to many different types of food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Zesting_an_orange.jpg/330px-Zesting_an_orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zest_(ingredient)"},{"title":"Citrus","blocks":[{"text":"Citrus is a genus of flowering trees and shrubs in the family Rutaceae. Plants in the genus produce citrus fruits, such as citrons, mandarins, and pomelos. Many important citrus crops have been developed through extensive hybridization, including oranges, lemons, grapefruits, and limes, all of which have many cultivars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/OrangeBloss_wb.jpg/330px-O